{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"930c62dea30ee4d4","name":"card_unit_kv_1s","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Homefront/units/card_unit_kv_1s","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"KV-1S","text":"Your other units have +1 attack for each of their combat keywords.","flavorText":"The KV-1S was an improved version of the Soviet KV-1 heavy tank, introduced in 1942 to address the original design's flaws. Early KV-1s had earned a reputation for their thick armor but suffered from excessive weight and mechanical breakdowns. The KV-1S, with the \"S\" standing for \"skorostnoi\" or \"fast,\" featured lighter armor, a redesigned turret, and a commander's cupola which improved visibility. These changes reduced the tank's weight by several tons, increasing its top speed to around 43 km/h. Although it sacrificed some armor protection, the KV-1S was more reliable and mobile on the battlefield. It remained armed with the same 76.2 mm gun as earlier models, which by 1943 was becoming less effective against newer German armor. As a result, the KV-1S was soon overshadowed by the S-series heavy tanks. Still, it saw service on multiple fronts through 1943 and into early 1944. Production of the KV-1S ended after 1,370 units were built. It marked the final major revision of the KV-1 before the Red Army shifted focus to more advanced designs like the IS-2.","faction":"Soviet","type":"tank","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_kv_1s","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_kv_1s_title","SourceString":"KV-1S","LocalizedString":"KV-1S"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":4,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_kv_1s_text","SourceString":"Your other units have +1 attack for each of their combat keywords.","LocalizedString":"Your other units have +1 attack for each of their combat keywords."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_kv_1s_history","SourceString":"The KV-1S was an improved version of the Soviet KV-1 heavy tank, introduced in 1942 to address the original design's flaws. Early KV-1s had earned a reputation for their thick armor but suffered from excessive weight and mechanical breakdowns. The KV-1S, with the \"S\" standing for \"skorostnoi\" or \"fast,\" featured lighter armor, a redesigned turret, and a commander's cupola which improved visibility. These changes reduced the tank's weight by several tons, increasing its top speed to around 43 km/h. Although it sacrificed some armor protection, the KV-1S was more reliable and mobile on the battlefield. It remained armed with the same 76.2 mm gun as earlier models, which by 1943 was becoming less effective against newer German armor. As a result, the KV-1S was soon overshadowed by the S-series heavy tanks. Still, it saw service on multiple fronts through 1943 and into early 1944. Production of the KV-1S ended after 1,370 units were built. It marked the final major revision of the KV-1 before the Red Army shifted focus to more advanced designs like the IS-2.","LocalizedString":"The KV-1S was an improved version of the Soviet KV-1 heavy tank, introduced in 1942 to address the original design's flaws. Early KV-1s had earned a reputation for their thick armor but suffered from excessive weight and mechanical breakdowns. The KV-1S, with the \"S\" standing for \"skorostnoi\" or \"fast,\" featured lighter armor, a redesigned turret, and a commander's cupola which improved visibility. These changes reduced the tank's weight by several tons, increasing its top speed to around 43 km/h. Although it sacrificed some armor protection, the KV-1S was more reliable and mobile on the battlefield. It remained armed with the same 76.2 mm gun as earlier models, which by 1943 was becoming less effective against newer German armor. As a result, the KV-1S was soon overshadowed by the S-series heavy tanks. Still, it saw service on multiple fronts through 1943 and into early 1944. Production of the KV-1S ended after 1,370 units were built. It marked the final major revision of the KV-1 before the Red Army shifted focus to more advanced designs like the IS-2."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLeaveBoardOrOwner","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAblitiesChanged"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::CombatKeywords"],"heavyArmor":1,"hasGuard":true,"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/KV-1S.KV-1S","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_kv_1s_photo","SourceString":"A column of KV-1S tanks. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"A column of KV-1S tanks. Date unknown."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionArmourM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionArmourM.36"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeMedium_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeMedium.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Tanks/BP_AttackTank.BP_AttackTank_C","SubPathString":""},"isHQDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"BuffedCards","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_kv_1s","owner":"card_unit_kv_1s_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"K2Node_Event_cardChanging","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in